The 68000 images a standalone build contains.

The Maven build writes the twenty-two here, as it writes them to build/68k
and into the classes the jar is made of, and they are committed: a module
fetched by its import path contains the files a commit has in it, so a
caller who runs `go get github.com/odipar/dtx/go` has the images an
executable embeds.

ImageTest reads them against a fresh assembly of 68k/, so an image that
does not match what rmac writes today fails the build.

A tree without them does not contain one, and Read then gives nil back: a
caller resolves an image as it otherwise would, out of build/68k beside
the templates DTX_68K names.
